{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Optimization.LPStrongDuality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Optimization.LPStrongDuality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Optimization.LPWeakDuality","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.lp_zero_duality_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.lp_zero_duality_gap","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L152-L158","doc":"**Zero duality gap** at an optimal primal point: the complementary optimal pair\n`(x, λ)` from `lp_strong_duality` has `dualityGap c x a λ = 0`. Conditional on\n`MatrixFarkas`; derived, sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.lp_strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.lp_strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L119-L150","doc":"**LP strong duality (Rivin math/9907032 Thm 3.2).** At a primal-optimal `x`\nthere is a **dual-optimal** `λ` whose objective equals the primal objective:\n`dualObj a λ = primalObj c x`. Hence the duality gap closes and `(x, λ)` is a\ncomplementary optimal pair.\n\nConditional on the Farkas class `[MatrixFarkas A a c]`; **fully derived, sorry-free**\nfrom it together with the unconditional `lp_weak_duality`. The Farkas field supplies\nthe `≥ γ` half (a dual certificate at the primal value), weak duality supplies the\n`≤ γ` half, and the two pin `dualObj a λ = primalObj c x`; dual optimality of `λ`\nthen follows from weak duality against every dual-feasible competitor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.lp_dual_feasible_of_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.lp_dual_feasible_of_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L107-L117","doc":"**A primal-feasible, bounded-below LP has a feasible dual** (`P*` is feasible).\nGiven any lower bound `v` on the primal objective over the feasible set, the Farkas\nalternative supplies a dual-feasible `λ` with `v ≤ aᵀλ`. Conditional on\n`MatrixFarkas`; derived, sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas.farkas_alternative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas.farkas_alternative","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Farkas / Gale theorem of the alternative (the open analytic input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas.mk","kind":"ctor","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas","kind":"class","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L85-L105","doc":"**The finite-dimensional Farkas / Gale alternative** for the standard-form LP\ndata `(A, a, c)` — the *analytic input* to strong duality, and the piece Mathlib\nlists as an open TODO (see the module docstring).\n\n`farkas_alternative γ` reads: *if the primal `{A x = a, x ≥ 0}` is feasible and no\nfeasible point attains objective `< γ` (so `γ` is a valid lower bound), then the\ndual `{λᵀA ≤ c}` has a point with objective `≥ γ`.* This is a genuine theorem of\nfinite-dimensional convex analysis (a transposition / theorem of the alternative,\nequivalent to strong duality); it is stated here as a hypothesis on the data, **not**\nproved. An instance of this class is understood as an appeal to Farkas' lemma, not as\na discharged proof obligation (§\"Axiomatization is NOT a Proof\", `AGENTS.md`).\n\nThe primal-feasibility guard is essential for *truth*: without it the statement is\nfalse when both primal and dual are infeasible (e.g. `A = 0, a ≠ 0, dual empty`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.DualOptimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.DualOptimal","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L79-L83","doc":"A dual point `λ` is **optimal** for `max aᵀλ s.t. λᵀA ≤ c` when it is feasible\nand no feasible point has larger objective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.PrimalOptimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.PrimalOptimal","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/LPStrongDuality.lean#L73-L77","doc":"A primal point `x` is **optimal** for `min cᵀx s.t. Ax = a, x ≥ 0` when it is\nfeasible and no feasible point has smaller objective. ","signatureChunk":0}]}